From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:05:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: secret-file guard asks less: don't ask again per
 project; loading into the environment isn't asked

- "Don't ask again for this file in this project": a 4th option in the
  guard's native dialog and in Mission Control's row. Remembered per project
  root + file in the profile prefs (meridian.workbench_secret_optouts), for
  every session and agent in that project. Settings > AI > Workbench lists
  the files with Remove buttons.
- A command that only loads secret files into the environment (source / .,
  with set -a or not; export $(grep -v '^#' F | xargs); env $(cat F | xargs)
  cmd; dotenv/dotenvx/env-cmd/direnv exec; --env-file for docker, node, npm)
  and prints nothing of them (no bare env/printenv/set/export -p/declare -p,
  no set -x, no echo of a secret-looking or file-defined variable, no inline
  interpreter code touching the environment) isn't held: the hook tells
  Meridian, which adds "Loaded <file> into the environment" to the session's
  Mission Control activity. Anything else still asks.
- The test dialog answer is read as UTF-8 (typographic apostrophes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
